00:27:57,900 --> 00:28:01,467
你曾经形容过在巴黎开车绕凯旋门环岛
是人生最大的冒险之一。
You did once describe driving
round the Arc de Triomphe
as life's great adventures.

561
00:28:01,500 --> 00:28:04,533
我超喜欢，简直刺激又吓人。
I love it. It's fantastically
frightening.

562
00:28:04,567 --> 00:28:07,267
我开福特GT试过一次，
那可真够呛。
I did it once in a Ford GT,
That was very tricky.

563
00:28:07,300 --> 00:28:08,667
福特GT是啥车？
What's a Ford GT?

564
00:28:08,700 --> 00:28:12,600
是一辆……
反正不是什么讨喜的车。
It's a...
Not a particularly nice car.

565
00:28:12,633 --> 00:28:15,900
对环境破坏挺严重的，
我其实不太喜欢它。
It damages
the environment quite badly.
I don't really like it.

566
00:28:15,933 --> 00:28:19,400
但有那么一瞬间，
当你刚杀到凯旋门转盘时，
But there is a moment
where you just get to
the Arc de Triomphe,

567
00:28:19,433 --> 00:28:21,733
-心里就会想：“来吧，走你！”
-我就爱这感觉。
-and just think, "Here we go!"
-I love it.

568
00:28:21,767 --> 00:28:25,233
太好玩了。过凯旋门的诀窍在于，
It's great fun. The trick
with the Arc de Triomphe,

569
00:28:25,267 --> 00:28:27,700
你绝对不能去看
谁正朝你撞过来。
you have to not look
who's coming at you.

570
00:28:27,733 --> 00:28:30,800
只管盯紧你要去哪儿，
而且一定要开一辆破破烂烂的破车。
Just look where you're going
and have a really badly,
beaten up car.

571
00:28:30,833 --> 00:28:32,733
没错，千万别开好车去受罪。
Yeah, never try it
in a nice car.

572
00:28:32,767 --> 00:28:35,533
越能弄到最烂的车越好，
那样所有人都会躲着你。
Always the worst car you can
lay your hands on.
Then everyone will avoid you.

573
00:28:35,567 --> 00:28:39,733
这也是为什么
我把你奉为“酷车墙”的灵感女神，
你懂我的意思吧。
This is one of the reasons
I've got you as the Cool Wall
muse, if you see what I mean.

574
00:28:39,767 --> 00:28:43,767
因为你在欧洲两头通吃，
在我眼里，你就是巴黎，就是欧洲。
Because, you do,
you straddle Europe. You're
Paris and Europe to me.

575
00:28:43,800 --> 00:28:47,733
比洛杉矶酷多了，
甚至比纽约还要酷。
It's just so much cooler
than Los Angeles
and even New York.

576
00:28:47,767 --> 00:28:51,533
但我能不能冒昧地拿几辆车
找你参谋参谋？
But do you mind awfully
if I just run a few
cars past you?

577
00:28:51,567 --> 00:28:53,433
-行啊。
-看看它们到底酷不酷。
-Yep.
-To establish their coolness.

578
00:28:53,467 --> 00:28:55,533
这辆。好的，很显然
这车非常酷。
This. Okay. Obviously
this is very cool.

579
00:28:55,567 --> 00:28:56,767
-没错。
-G-Wiz。
-Yes.
-G-Wiz.

580
00:28:56,800 --> 00:28:57,867
哈蒙德：啥？！
HAMMOND: What!

581
00:28:57,900 --> 00:28:59,533
不过我今天没戴眼镜。
I haven't got
my specs on though.

582
00:28:59,567 --> 00:29:02,433
不好意思老兄，
你去年还说它长得像个“肉瘤”呢。
Sorry, mate. You described it
as a "wart" last year.

583
00:29:03,833 --> 00:29:05,400
它挺好看的啊，
真的很漂亮。
It is beautiful.
It is beautiful.

584
00:29:05,433 --> 00:29:09,367
你唯一可能遇到的问题，
就是怎么钻进去。
The only problem
that you might find
is getting into it.

585
00:29:09,400 --> 00:29:14,767
而且在下雨的晚上，
你只能在雨刷和大灯之间二选一。
And on a rainy night, you
have to choose between
windscreen wipers and lights.

586
00:29:14,800 --> 00:29:17,933
你看，
宣传册上可没写这出。
You see,
that isn't in the brochure.

587
00:29:17,967 --> 00:29:20,200
不过我想澄清一下，我说它是肉瘤的时候，
But I would like to say,
when I said it was a wart

588
00:29:20,233 --> 00:29:23,400
我想表达的意思，其实更偏向
辛迪·克劳馥嘴角的“美人痣”。
I was thinking more
in terms of Cindy Crawford's
beauty spot.

589
00:29:23,433 --> 00:29:27,167
我爱这车，我绝对爱死它了。
在伦敦开简直无敌，所以……
I love this car. I absolutely
love this car. It's absolutely
brilliant for London. So...

590
00:29:27,200 --> 00:29:29,367
-非常感谢，所以它非常酷。
-非常、非常、非常酷。
-Thank you very much.
And that's very cool.
-Very, very, very cool.

591
00:29:29,400 --> 00:29:34,067
我们之前在酷车墙上经常预判，
既然你住在巴黎，
Now we've often said, on the
Cool Wall that we anticipate,
because you live in Paris,

592
00:29:34,067 --> 00:29:36,600
那这种欧洲小车，看到没？
that small European cars
like those, okay?

593
00:29:36,633 --> 00:29:40,767
雷诺，还有那辆小雪铁龙，
还有这辆小菲亚特，都很酷。
Renault, and that's
a little Citroen, and that's
a little Fiat. They're cool.

594
00:29:40,800 --> 00:29:42,067
嗯。
Yeah.

595
00:29:42,100 --> 00:29:44,667
-我们说的对吧？
-对，我觉得雷诺挺酷的。
-Are we right?
-Yes, I think
the Renaults are.

596
00:29:44,700 --> 00:29:46,700
-菲亚特不酷？
-那辆。
-Not the Fiat?
-That one.

597
00:29:46,733 --> 00:29:49,067
-那辆小的？
-那辆屁股看着有点别扭。
-The little one?
-That one's a bit dodgy
at the back.

598
00:29:49,067 --> 00:29:51,533
-有点啥？别扭？
-我不喜欢车尾，方头方脑的……
-A bit what? Dodgy?
-I don't like the back,
it's sort of square...

599
00:29:51,567 --> 00:29:52,833
克拉克森：对，我知道，我同意。
CLARKSON: Yeah I know,
I agree.

600
00:29:52,867 --> 00:29:56,633
垃圾，纯粹的工业垃圾。
菲亚特Punto就是破烂货。
Crap, absolute crap.
Fiat Puntos are rubbish.

601
00:29:56,667 --> 00:29:59,900
能有人悄悄过去把它挪到底下吗？
太恶心了。
Would somebody quietly go and
move it down? Just awful.

602
00:29:59,933 --> 00:30:03,267
而且我们以前还说过这种话。
And we've also said
this kind of thing.

603
00:30:03,300 --> 00:30:05,467
- 红色宾利。
- 我超爱那个，快拿给我看。
-Red Bentley.
-I love that. Show it to me.

604
00:30:08,033 --> 00:30:10,000
你现在感觉如何？
How do you feel now?

605
00:30:10,033 --> 00:30:13,833
我以前可能不小心说过，
那是柴郡足球暴发户开的车。
I may have accidentally
said in the past that it's
a Cheshire footballer's car.

606
00:30:13,867 --> 00:30:16,100
- 可它本来就是！
- 怎么，那车很酷吗？
-But it is!
-What, that's cool?

607
00:30:16,133 --> 00:30:20,600
太精彩了。你苦心经营四年的
“酷车墙”
刚才彻底毁于一旦。
That's fabulous. Four years
of your Cool Wall
has just been destroyed.

608
00:30:22,200 --> 00:30:24,900
上周我们拿电锯锯它，
你倒好，直接端机枪扫射了。
We took a chainsaw to it
last week.
You're machine-gunning it.

609
00:30:24,933 --> 00:30:26,300
红色宾利挺合我意的。
A red Bentley would do.

610
00:30:26,333 --> 00:30:28,367
- 四驱越野车呢？
- 我不太喜欢那种。
-Four-wheel drive cars?
-I don't really like those.

611
00:30:28,400 --> 00:30:30,900
漂亮！我上周把它们
全扔到底下去了。
Yes! I moved them all down
last week.

612
00:30:30,933 --> 00:30:32,900
- 我以前有一辆，后来处理掉了。
- 是吗？
-I used to have one
and I got rid of it.
-Did you?

613
00:30:32,933 --> 00:30:36,800
- 你以前开哪款？
- 我那辆挺不错的。
是辆挺大的沃尔沃什么来着。
-Which one did you have?
-I had a really nice one.
It was a big Volvo something.

614
00:30:37,900 --> 00:30:39,800
- XC90？
- 我哪搞得清楚啊，亲爱的。
-XC90?
-I have no idea, darling.

615
00:30:39,833 --> 00:30:42,700
- 我就有一辆那个！
- 就是那种块头特大的。
-I've got one of those?
-You know those
really huge ones.

616
00:30:42,733 --> 00:30:45,467
- 我还挺喜欢的……
- 对，里面有七个座儿？
-I liked it...
-Yeah. There were
seven seats in it?

617
00:30:45,500 --> 00:30:47,767
- 没错，就是它。
- 我开的就是那款。
-Yes. That's right.
-That's what I've got.

618
00:30:47,800 --> 00:30:49,567
出生年份跟……
Born in the same year...

619
00:30:49,600 --> 00:30:51,833
别提了……谢谢啊。
Don't... Thank you.

620
00:30:54,667 --> 00:30:58,633
……理查德·哈蒙德一样，不过……
我刚才总算圆过去了。
...as Richard Hammond, but...
I got out of that one.

621
00:30:58,667 --> 00:31:02,667
好了，能让我提一下劳斯莱斯吗？
Right, can I just say
Rolls Royce?

622
00:31:02,700 --> 00:31:06,067
呃，我对劳斯莱斯态度有点微妙。
Um, I'm slightly ambivalent
about Rolls Royces.

623
00:31:06,067 --> 00:31:09,133
- 没错，理查德·哈蒙德今天早上就是坐一辆来的……
- 鬼扯！
-Yeah, Richard Hammond came
down in one this morning...
-What!

624
00:31:09,933 --> 00:31:12,300
他现在开始满嘴跑火车了！
Now he's lying!

625
00:31:12,333 --> 00:31:15,800
- 伙计，我看你刚才算是出了个大丑。
- 这纯属垂死挣扎！
-Guess you made a bit of a
fool of yourself there, mate.
-This is desperate!

626
00:31:15,833 --> 00:31:17,700
早就跟你说了不该提的。
Told you
shouldn't have done it.

627
00:31:17,733 --> 00:31:21,667
现在，最重磅的来了，
兰博基尼Gallardo Spyder。
Now, most important,
Lamborghini Gallardo Spyder.

628
00:31:21,700 --> 00:31:25,067
- 这个嘛……是的。
- 怎么了？
-This is... Yeah.
-What?

629
00:31:26,067 --> 00:31:27,933
哎，那车弱爆了，不是吗？
Well, it's pathetic, isn't it?

630
00:31:27,967 --> 00:31:29,967
（欢呼声）
(CHEERING)

631
00:31:36,467 --> 00:31:38,867
要是谁手上有把刀的话……
If anybody's got a knife...

632
00:31:39,400 --> 00:31:41,700
得嘞，那退了吧。
Right, so, cancel that.

633
00:31:41,733 --> 00:31:44,367
- 啥，退订？
- 对。
-What, order?
-Yes.

634
00:31:44,400 --> 00:31:46,733
- 你订了这车？
- 没。
-Have you got one of these?
-Nope.

635
00:31:48,800 --> 00:31:51,267
我以为你会像个正经人一样开沃尔沃。
I thought you had a Volvo
like a sensible person.

636
00:31:51,300 --> 00:31:53,333
- 开什么？
- 沃尔沃。
-A what?
-A Volvo.

637
00:31:53,367 --> 00:31:56,600
孩子们平时坐沃尔沃，因为他们要上下学，
The children go round in
a Volvo and because they're
going to school and back,

638
00:31:56,633 --> 00:31:59,667
我必须得换辆别的开开，我还以为那车会挺……
I had to have something else
and I thought that would be,

639
00:31:59,700 --> 00:32:01,567
烂透了，我真不知道该说什么……
rubbish and I don't know
what...

640
00:32:01,600 --> 00:32:04,233
现在，请允许我继续往下说。
Now, if I may, I'll move on.

641
00:32:04,267 --> 00:32:07,067
-因为你来这儿
是为了主演话剧《海鸥》。
-出演《海鸥》。
-Because you're over here
starring in The Seagull.
-In The Seagull.

642
00:32:07,067 --> 00:32:08,500
契诃夫的名作。
The Chekov play.

643
00:32:08,533 --> 00:32:10,867
-不过《海鸥》讲的可不是海鸥。
-确实不是。
-Now, The Seagull's
not about a seagull.
-No.

644
00:32:10,900 --> 00:32:13,400
-你想知道讲的是什么吗？
-我想我可能……
-Do you want to know
what it's about?
-I think I might...

645
00:32:13,433 --> 00:32:14,933
能让我猜猜看吗？碰碰运气。
Can I just guess? Just to see.

646
00:32:14,967 --> 00:32:18,500
第一幕，平平淡淡。
第二幕，还是平淡。
Act one, not much happens.
Act two, not much.

647
00:32:18,533 --> 00:32:20,067
-第三幕……
-大事爆发了？
-Act three...
-Everything happens?

648
00:32:20,067 --> 00:32:21,633
其实是在幕间休息的时候，
有人跑了出去，
Well, it's in between
the acts,
somebody goes off

649
00:32:21,667 --> 00:32:22,833
企图冲自己的脑袋开一枪，
and tries to shoot
themselves in the head

650
00:32:22,867 --> 00:32:24,667
-结果还没打中。
-还没打中。
-and then misses.
-And misses.

651
00:32:24,700 --> 00:32:26,433
所以大家都在酒吧里呆着，
接着他回来了，
That's why everyone's
in the bar and then he
comes back

652
00:32:26,467 --> 00:32:28,800
-脑袋上还缠着一圈绷带。
-没错。
-and he's got a bandage
on his head.
-Yes.

653
00:32:28,833 --> 00:32:30,933
-这剧的门票全卖光了。
-是啊。
-This is completely sold out.
-Yeah.

654
00:32:30,967 --> 00:32:34,467
一张票都搞不到，
天知道我费了多大劲去抢。
You can't get tickets
and God knows I've tried.

655
00:32:34,500 --> 00:32:37,200
-你对契诃夫情有独钟？
-我就是特别喜欢契诃夫。
-Have you got a thing
about Chekhov?
-I just really like Chekhov.

656
00:32:37,233 --> 00:32:39,300
没有，我对契诃夫倒没啥执念，
No, I haven't got
a thing about Chekhov,

657
00:32:39,333 --> 00:32:41,767
只是觉得，呃……
（叹气）
but I just find that, uh.
(SIGHS)

658
00:32:41,800 --> 00:32:45,133
那个……
好吧，我一共也就演过两部话剧。
The...
Well, I've only done
two plays.

659
00:32:45,167 --> 00:32:47,900
我是不是已经把你聊烦了？
Am I boring you already?

660
00:32:54,933 --> 00:32:56,400
真会说话。
So smooth.

661
00:32:56,433 --> 00:32:58,900
克拉克森：才不是，可悲透了。
CLARKSON: It's not.
It's pathetic.

662
00:32:58,933 --> 00:33:00,600
我好感动。
I'm touched.

663
00:33:00,633 --> 00:33:02,700
如果有人想来主持 Top Gear，
If anybody wants a job
presenting Top Gear,

664
00:33:02,733 --> 00:33:07,067
请寄信到：伦敦 W12 7TS，伍德巷，BBC。
the address is BBC, Wood Lane,
London W12 7TS.

665
00:33:07,067 --> 00:33:10,433
现在，显然我们马上就能看到
你的单圈成绩到底如何了。
And now, we're gonna find out,
obviously, in a minute
how your lap was.

666
00:33:10,467 --> 00:33:12,867
想先跟我们透露一下跑得怎样吗？
Do you want to tell us
how it went?

667
00:33:12,900 --> 00:33:14,933
中间好像有一段陷进泥里了，是吧？
There was a bit of a
boggy moment, wasn't there?

668
00:33:14,967 --> 00:33:17,467
-你冲出赛道了？
-我冲出去了，还陷进去了。
-Did you go off?
-I went off and sunk.

669
00:33:17,500 --> 00:33:18,967
真的吗？真的。
Really? Yes.

670
00:33:19,067 --> 00:33:21,667
我看到一辆救护车朝着我飞驰而来。
I saw an ambulance come
speeding towards me.

671
00:33:21,700 --> 00:33:25,833
不是为了救我，
纯粹只是要把车从烂泥里拖出来。
Not to rescue me but just to
tow the car out of the mud.

672
00:33:25,867 --> 00:33:28,067
你是开太快了，还是迷路了？
Were you going too fast
or get lost?

673
00:33:28,067 --> 00:33:30,100
呃，都不是，我基本上就是放弃打方向盘了。
Well, no, I just sort of
gave up steering.

674
00:33:32,467 --> 00:33:34,867
这么着吧，
有谁想看她的圈速？
I tell you what,
who'd like to see the lap?

675
00:33:34,900 --> 00:33:36,467
观众：想看！
AUDIENCE: Yes.

676
00:33:36,500 --> 00:33:38,200
好，上录像！
Okay, let's play the tape.

677
00:33:38,233 --> 00:33:40,400
（轮胎尖叫声）
(TYRES SCREECHING)

678
00:33:40,433 --> 00:33:41,800
克拉克森：巴黎式起步。
CLARKSON: Parisian start.

679
00:33:41,833 --> 00:33:44,067
（唱着调）
太阳晃瞎我眼睛啦！
(SING-SONGY)
The sun's in my eyes!

680
00:33:44,067 --> 00:33:46,300
克拉克森：噢，看着不错。
托马斯：我还唱歌呢。
CLARKSON: Oh, looks good.
THOMAS: I sing.

681
00:33:46,333 --> 00:33:49,933
这开得既丝滑又挑不出毛病。
我反正是看不出
有任何问题。
This is smooth and perfect
in every way. I can't see
anything wrong with that.

682
00:33:53,067 --> 00:33:55,067
-切进芝加哥弯，接着又是……
-（轮胎尖叫声）
-And into Chicago and again...
-(TYRES SCREECHING)

683
00:33:55,067 --> 00:33:56,767
没得说，绝对精准无误。
No, absolutely bang on.

684
00:33:58,967 --> 00:34:02,067
休·格兰特当时也是这么开的。
然后……
Hugh Grant did that.
And then...

685
00:34:02,067 --> 00:34:04,833
我刹车踩得不够狠。
真是见鬼！
I'm not braking hard enough.
Bloody hell!

686
00:34:05,900 --> 00:34:07,500
克拉克森：
然后，这又是哪一出？
CLARKSON:
And then, what's this?

687
00:34:07,533 --> 00:34:10,433
看得出你在这儿冲出赛道了。
到处都是烂泥。
I can see where you've been
off there. It's awfully muddy.

688
00:34:10,467 --> 00:34:12,500
到这里了。你过这里时
是全油门冲过去的吗？
Now here. Did you go fast
flat-out through here?

